      "problem": "Is \n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/foundations/14142331/assets/4077efc3b3c0463daf06fb0e8688d29725154980b2350f8b4db7c2b584b4df96.svg)\nan elementary matrix?",
      "worked_solution": "Remember that an elementary matrix is obtained by performing exactly one elementary row operation on the identity matrix $I.$\n\nThe given matrix $E$ is an elementary matrix because it can be obtained from $I$ by applying the elementary row operation $R_2 := R_2 + 8R_1,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+8{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 8 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =E\\end{aligned}\n$$",
